      "hints": [
        "Differentiate $y = (5x - 1)^{1/2}$ using the chain rule: $\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{5x - 1}}$.",
        "Use $\\frac{dy}{dt} = \\frac{dy}{dx} \\times \\frac{dx}{dt}$ with $\\frac{dx}{dt} = 2$ and $x = 1$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Differentiate $y = (5x - 1)^{1/2}$ with respect to $x$ using the chain rule:\n$$\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{1}{2}(5x - 1)^{-1/2} \\times (5) = \\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{5x - 1}}$$",
        "Evaluate $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at $x = 1$:\n$$\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=1} = \\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{5(1) - 1}} = \\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{4}} = \\frac{5}{4}$$",
        "Apply the chain rule for rates of change with $\\frac{dx}{dt} = 2\\text{ units/min}$:\n$$\\frac{dy}{dt} = \\frac{dy}{dx} \\times \\frac{dx}{dt} = \\frac{5}{4} \\times 2 = \\frac{5}{2} = 2.5\\text{ units per minute}$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Rates of Change": "Differentiates to $\\frac{5}{2}(5x - 1)^{-1/2}$ (B2). Applies chain rule at $x=1$ (M1). Obtains $\\frac{5}{2}\\text{ units/min}$ (A1)."
        },
